# `render` before another operator: DS0120, with a fix that moves it to the end.
mode: syntax
---- query
from 'orders.csv' | render barchart | take 5
---- expected
PROGRAM@0..45
  PIPELINE@0..44
    IDENT@0..4 "from"
    WHITESPACE@4..5 " "
    LITERAL@5..17
      STRING@5..17 "'orders.csv'"
    WHITESPACE@17..18 " "
    PIPE@18..19 "|"
    WHITESPACE@19..20 " "
    RENDER_OP@20..35
      IDENT@20..26 "render"
      WHITESPACE@26..27 " "
      IDENT@27..35 "barchart"
    WHITESPACE@35..36 " "
    PIPE@36..37 "|"
    WHITESPACE@37..38 " "
    TAKE_OP@38..44
      IDENT@38..42 "take"
      WHITESPACE@42..43 " "
      LITERAL@43..44
        LONG@43..44 "5"
  WHITESPACE@44..45 "\n"

error[DS0120]: `render` must be the last operator
  --> query:1:21
  |
1 | from 'orders.csv' | render barchart | take 5
  |                     ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^   ------ this operator comes after `render`
  |                     |
  |                     the chart is drawn at this point
  |
  = help: move `render barchart` to the end of the query

with the machine-applicable fixes applied:
    from 'orders.csv' | take 5 | render barchart
which parses without errors
